NOT PROVEN BY THIS READ (stated so it is not read as proven):
  1. This is the authorizer's code and the handler's code. No real INTERNAL session's JWT was decoded here, so "an internal login's JWT carries tier=internal" rests on the authorizer's own `tier==="internal"` test. The step-9 post-act read is what measures it.
  2. The authorizer also grants ALL access to `userType==="Dev"` whatever its `tier` (q2). A Dev-type login whose tier is not exactly "internal" would be admitted by the authorizer and refused (403) by the fenced handler. Not a blocker for this order (the ruling fences on tier==internal exactly); filed as surprise row AMGT_HARVST-D1-S9 for the issuer.
